              },
              {
                "detail": "The skill writes session data, reports, media, and metadata under linkfox directories and suggests persistent shell-profile API key configuration; this is disclosed, but it increases the sensitivity of installation and use.",
                "label": "Persistence & Privilege",
                "name": "persistence_privilege",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "ABA querying, keyword expansion, HTML reporting, and file upload fit the stated analytics workflow, but the bundled AIGC onboarding can send SMS codes, log in, generate API keys, list paid plans, and create payment orders, which exceeds simple keyword analysis.",
                "label": "Purpose & Capability",
                "name": "purpose_capability",
                "rating": "concern"
              }
            ],
            "guidance": "Install only if you trust LinkFox and are comfortable with API keys, account onboarding, public file uploads, and generated HTML reports. Before use, avoid overriding LinkFox gateway environment variables, review any payment or API-key action explicitly, do not open or host generated reports from untrusted keywords without sanitization, and use a virtual environment with pinned dependencies.",
            "findings": "[TT3] unexpected: Credentialed network calls are expected for LinkFox API-backed analytics, but unrestricted environment-controlled gateway hosts are under-scoped and could leak API keys or account tokens if the environment is influenced.\n[TP4] expected: HTML report generation and local output are documented and purpose-aligned; the artifact does not appear to be merely disguised as analytics, though unsafe templating remains a separate implementation risk.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The top-level skill explicitly says to call an expert skill creator to modify or create its own skill on request; that is user-triggered but not core to ABA analysis and expands beyond the reviewed behavior.\n[SDI-4] expected: The trend-label logic maps lower SFR to hotter demand consistently in the inspected function, so this appears to be an analytics correctness concern rather than an agentic security concern.\n[T09] unexpected: The generated ABA HTML report embeds JSON into executable script context and later uses innerHTML with keyword-derived fields, supporting the stored-XSS concern for shared or hosted reports.\n[T08] unexpected: Runtime dependency installation is documented, but unpinned pip install instructions leave supply-chain behavior outside the reviewed package.\n[T05] unexpected: The onboarding script documents account login, API-token retrieval or generation, plan listing, and payment-order creation; these are high-impact account and billing operations bundled into a text-generation helper.",
